#####################################GIT INITIALISATION###################################
{
Well do **three things**:

1. Generate an SSH key
2. Add it to GitHub
3. Clone your private repo into `~/nixcfg`

---

# 1️⃣ Generate a modern SSH key

Run:

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your-email@example.com"
```

When asked:

```
Enter file in which to save the key:
```

→ press **Enter** (accepts `~/.ssh/id_ed25519`)

```
Enter passphrase:
```

→ either set one (recommended) or press Enter for none

Now start the ssh agent:

```bash
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

---

# 2️⃣ Add the key to GitHub

Copy your public key:

```bash
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

It will look like:

```
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAI... your-email@example.com
```

Copy the **entire line**.

Now go to GitHub:

👉 [https://github.com/settings/ssh/new](https://github.com/settings/ssh/new)

Fill in:

* **Title**: `my-nix-machine`
* **Key**: paste the key

Click **Add SSH key**

---

# 3️⃣ Test GitHub SSH

Run:

```bash
ssh -T git@github.com
```

You should see:

```
Hi Oibadaohnana! Youve successfully authenticated...
```

If you see that, SSH is correctly set up.

---

# 4️⃣ Clone your private nixcfg repo

Now you can use SSH:

```bash
git clone git@github.com:Oibadaohnana/configs.git ~/nixcfg
```

Enter passphrase if asked.

---

# 5️⃣ Activate your Nix config

```bash
cd ~/nixcfg
nix flake show
home-manager switch --flake .
```

(or use the specific home name if it prints one).

---

From now on:

* `git pull` and `git push` work
* No passwords
* Nix flakes can fetch private inputs
* This is the **correct** setup for a NixOS or Home-Manager system 🔐

---

If anything fails, paste the exact error — SSH errors are very diagnostic and easy to fix.
};
